---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { route } from '../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Cookies on Stamp Duty Australia: what this site stores and why" description="Cookies on this stamp duty site: none. Stability is monitored anonymously with Microsoft Clarity in cookie-free mode; what the share link holds and how to clear it." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Cookies' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Cookies</h1>
    <p>No page of the site sets a cookie, advertising or otherwise. The calculators run in your browser and keep nothing once the tab is closed.</p>
    <h2>Anonymous stability monitoring</h2>
    <p>To find broken pages, script errors, slow loading and buttons that do not respond, the site loads Microsoft Clarity, from Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited, in its cookie-free mode. Clarity then sets no cookie (no <code>_clck</code>, <code>_clsk</code>, <code>MUID</code> or <code>CLID</code>), gives every page view a one-off identifier and does not link visits. The price, state and buyer details you enter, and page content, are masked before anything is sent. As nothing is stored on your device, there is no cookie banner. Blocking the clarity.ms domain stops this monitoring without affecting the calculators.</p>
    <p>The <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a> explains who receives the monitoring data and for how long.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
